Apple <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/introducing-apple-home-collection-a-new-lineup-of-smart-home-accessories/">today debuted</a> the "Apple Home Collection," an accessory lineup it developed with LG Electronics and Schneider Electric. The collection includes cameras, thermostats, temperature sensors, and a door lock.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-home-collection.jpg" alt="" width="1960" height="1102" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070337" /><br/>
All of the home devices are designed to work with the HomeView, Apple's new home hub. Apple says each one is made from premium materials with a minimal aesthetic. The accessories are able to be set up with a single tap from the iPhone, and can be controlled with the Home app and through <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>.<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Video Doorbell (&#36;249.95)</strong> - The Video Doorbell has dual cameras that capture views of visitors and packages. The front camera has a 2.5K resolution and the bottom camera is HD resolution. It has a built-in spotlight and a chime that plays through HomeView, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a>, or &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; mini.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Outdoor Cam (&#36;299.95)</strong> - The Outdoor Cam has low-color night vision and can be angled in multiple positions.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Indoor Cam (&#36;199.95)</strong> - The Indoor Cam has a privacy-preserving feature that allows it to tilt up when people are in the home so it's not recording, and down when people leave for keeping an eye on the home. The tilt function works based on geofencing, but can also be controlled in the Home app or manually.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Floodlight Cam (&#36;399.95)</strong> - The Floodlight Cam has dual floodlights that activate when motion is detected and low-color night vision.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Smart Deadbolt Lock (&#36;349.95)</strong> - The lock has UWB and can unlock automatically when the homeowner approaches, with no tap required. It also supports unlocking via PIN or a hidden backup key slot, and there is detection for whether the door is opened, closed, or has been tampered with. The doorbell and lock can work together as one, letting users see who is at the door and unlocking it if needed.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>LG Thermostat (&#36;199.95)</strong> - The thermostat supports Adaptive Temperature and in the U.S., heating and cooling can be activated during lower-cost periods for users with a compatible utility plan. The thermostat can read temperature and humidity across multiple rooms using separate temperature and humidity sensors. Sensors are priced at &#36;39.95.</li><br/>
 	<li><strong>Schneider Electric Thermostat (&#36;199.95)</strong> - Also supports Adaptive Temperature and can be used with temperature and humidity sensors. Sensors are priced at &#36;39.95.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Cameras work with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/icloud/">iCloud</a>+ plans and users can view live footage and camera activity from the Home app on iPhone, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>, Mac, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> 4K, and HomeView.<br/>
<br/>
